<h2 id="crystalline-section-introduction" class="tex-section"><span data-tag="07GJ">60.1</span> Introduction</h2>

<p>
This chapter is based on a lecture series given by Johan de Jong held in 2012 at Columbia University. The goals of this chapter are to give a quick introduction to crystalline cohomology. A reference is the book <span class="cite">[<a href="/bibliography/Berthelot">Berthelot</a>]</span>. 
</p>
<p>
We have moved the more elementary purely algebraic discussion of divided power rings to a preliminary chapter as it is also useful in discussing Tate resolutions in commutative algebra. Please see Divided Power Algebra, Section <a href="/tag/09PE" data-tag="09PE">23.1</a>. 
</p>
